      intro: 'Interpolation is how a template shows a value from its class. You write the field name inside double curly braces, and Rangular puts the current value on the screen. When the field changes, the screen updates on its own. Try it in the demo below: type in the box and watch the greeting mirror what you type, letter by letter. The box carries your typing into the field with [(ngModel)]; ngModel gets its own lesson later, in the forms batch, and interpolation is the half to watch here.',
      code: '<h1>Hello, {{ name }}</h1>',
