      intro: 'Lesson 5 met ngIf. This lesson goes deeper: conditions can compare and combine, like count >= 5 or signedIn && hasMail, and a ternary inside interpolation picks between two texts. One honest limit: Angular writes an else branch as *ngIf="ready; else loading". Rangular does not generate that yet. It warns with the diagnostic GEN_NGIF_ELSE_TODO and shows the block all the time, which is wrong on screen, so do not use it. The Rangular way is a pair: one block with *ngIf="ready" and a second block with *ngIf="!ready". The demo uses that pair for its sign in panel.',
      code: '<p *ngIf="signedIn">Welcome back</p>\n<p *ngIf="!signedIn">Please sign in</p>',
