      intro: 'In Angular, a template can bind classes and single styles: [class.alert]="hasError" turns one class on and off, [style.color] sets one style, and [ngClass] and [ngStyle] take whole objects of them. In Rangular, the single class toggle is wired: declare the class in the component\'s CSS file, the one the styleUrls array names, and bind it with [class.look-highlight], and it turns on and off live, as the last line of the demo shows. The whole-object and single-style forms, [class], [ngClass], [style.color] and [ngStyle], are not wired. The compiler now warns about them (GEN_CLASS_BINDING and GEN_STYLE_BINDING) and names the working pattern, instead of letting them fail silently as it once did. For a whole look that changes with state, write named classes in that CSS file and swap which pre-styled block shows with ngIf, exactly as the three look lines in the demo do.',
      code: '<p class="look-sunny" *ngIf="look === \'sunny\'">The garden in the sun.</p>\n<p [class.look-highlight]="highlighted">This flower bed carries a class binding.</p>',
      implementation: '// class-style.component.ts\nimport { Component } from \'@angular/core\';\n\n@Component({\n  selector: \'app-class-style-demo\',\n  templateUrl: \'./class-style.component.html\',\n  styleUrls: [\'./class-style.component.css\'],\n})\nexport class ClassStyleDemoComponent {\n  look = \'sunny\';\n  highlighted = false;\n  ownLine = \'My own flower\';\n\n  show(look: string) {\n    this.look = look;\n  }\n\n  toggleHighlight() {\n    this.highlighted = !this.highlighted;\n  }\n}\n\n// class-style.component.html\n<p class="look-sunny" *ngIf="look === \'sunny\'">The garden in the sun.</p>\n<p class="look-rainy" *ngIf="look === \'rainy\'">The garden in the rain.</p>\n<p class="look-big" *ngIf="look === \'big\'">The garden, up close.</p>\n<button (click)="show(\'sunny\')">\n  Sunny\n</button>\n<button (click)="show(\'rainy\')">\n  Rainy\n</button>\n<button (click)="show(\'big\')">\n  Big\n</button>\n<p [class.look-highlight]="highlighted">This flower bed carries a class binding. The highlight class turns on and off with the button below.</p>\n<button (click)="toggleHighlight()">\n  Toggle highlight\n</button>\n<input label="Try it: your own garden line, in all three looks" [(ngModel)]="ownLine">\n<p class="look-sunny">{{ ownLine }}</p>\n<p class="look-rainy">{{ ownLine }}</p>\n<p class="look-big">{{ ownLine }}</p>\n\n// class-style.component.css\n.look-sunny { color: #b07d10; font-weight: 700; }\n.look-rainy { color: #546e7a; }\n.look-big { font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; }\n.look-highlight { background-color: #fef7e0; }',
