      intro: 'A child rarely hard codes everything. The parent passes data down through inputs: fields on the child marked with @Input(). In the parent template you bind them like properties, [name]="flowerName", and when the parent value changes, the child renders again with the new value. The demo is the flower from the last lesson, grown into a card: the garden hands it a name and a petal colour. Tap Next flower and the garden cycles through three flowers; the card follows at once, because the input is a live binding, not a copy made once.',
      code: '<app-flower-card\n  [name]="flowerName"\n  [colour]="flowerColour">\n</app-flower-card>',
      implementation: '// inputs.component.ts\nimport { Component } from \'@angular/core\';\nimport { FlowerCardComponent } from \'./flower-card.component\';\n\n@Component({\n  selector: \'app-inputs-demo\',\n  templateUrl: \'./inputs.component.html\',\n})\nexport class InputsDemoComponent {\n  private flowers = [\n    { name: \'Sunflower\', colour: \'gold\' },\n    { name: \'Rose\', colour: \'red\' },\n    { name: \'Tulip\', colour: \'pink\' },\n  ];\n  private index = 0;\n  flowerName = \'Sunflower\';\n  flowerColour = \'gold\';\n\n  cycle() {\n    this.index = (this.index + 1) % this.flowers.length;\n    this.flowerName = this.flowers[this.index].name;\n    this.flowerColour = this.flowers[this.index].colour;\n  }\n}\n\n// flower-card.component.ts\nimport { Component, Input } from \'@angular/core\';\n\n@Component({\n  selector: \'app-flower-card\',\n  templateUrl: \'./flower-card.component.html\',\n})\nexport class FlowerCardComponent {\n  @Input() name = \'\';\n  @Input() colour = \'\';\n}\n\n// inputs.component.html\n<app-flower-card [name]="flowerName" [colour]="flowerColour"></app-flower-card>\n<button (click)="cycle()">\n  Next flower\n</button>\n\n// flower-card.component.html\n<h3>\n  Hello, I am a {{ name }}\n</h3>\n<p>My petals are {{ colour }}</p>',
