      intro: 'Inputs flow down. Outputs flow up. A child marks a field with @Output() and gives it an EventEmitter. When something happens inside the child, it calls emit with a value. The parent listens with round brackets, (picked)="recordPick($event)", and $event is exactly the value the child sent. The demo flower is the card from the last lesson, with one new power: a Pick this flower button. Every pick emits the flower name; the garden counts the picks and shows the last flower it received.',
      diagram: '+------------------------------+\n| Child: FlowerPickComponent   |\n| the Pick button is tapped    |\n+---------------+--------------+\n                |\n     picked.emit(this.name)\n                |\n                v\n+------------------------------+\n| Parent template              |\n| (picked)="recordPick($event)"|\n+---------------+--------------+\n                |\n                v\n+------------------------------+\n| Garden (the parent)          |\n| recordPick(name) runs:       |\n| pickCount++                  |\n| lastPicked = name            |\n+------------------------------+',
      code: '<app-flower-pick\n  *ngFor="let f of flowers"\n  [name]="f"\n  (picked)="recordPick($event)">\n</app-flower-pick>',
